# Story 1.0. Secrets come from the platform secret store in every real
# environment; this file documents the variables, never their values.

CELL_NAME=local-eu-west-1

# ---- ports ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Published host ports. Chosen to stay clear of a machine that already runs
# Postgres on 5432 (and, commonly, Redis on 6379).
#   API_PORT is also the port the API LISTENS on, container or host.
#   POSTGRES_PORT / REDIS_PORT are HOST mappings only - inside the compose
#   network those services keep 5432 and 6379, where nothing can collide.
API_PORT=3001
CONSOLE_PORT=8081
POSTGRES_PORT=5433
REDIS_PORT=6380
PORT=3001

# ---- datastores -------------------------------------------------------------
# Running the API on the HOST against the compose datastores? Use the published
# ports (5433 / 6380). Running it INSIDE compose? docker-compose.yml already
# points it at postgres:5432 and redis:6379 over the container network.
DATABASE_URL_ADMIN=postgres://postgres@127.0.0.1:5433/jazzticketing
DATABASE_URL_APP=postgres://jt_app:jt_app_local_only@127.0.0.1:5433/jazzticketing
REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6380

# Set from the platform secret store in any real environment; ops/migrate.ts
# rotates the application role's password to this value.
APP_DB_PASSWORD=

# The fixture auth stub is Story 1.0 only and must never be 1 outside local/CI.
# Story 1.5 removes its production path.
FIXTURE_AUTH=0

# ---- the Jazzware-internal surface (Stories 11.1, 1.1) ----------------------
# The control plane connects as its OWN database role, granted nothing in the
# cell schema, so an operator session cannot read tenant data even if a handler
# asks it to (migration 004).
DATABASE_URL_CONTROL=postgres://jt_control:jt_control_local_only@127.0.0.1:5433/jazzticketing
CONTROL_DB_PASSWORD=

# A DIFFERENT secret from the cell's. Set from the platform secret store in any
# real environment; if the two are ever set alike, the token audience check is
# what still keeps an operator token out of a cell (negative control 23).
CONTROL_PLANE_TOKEN_SECRET=

# The FIRST operator account is a deployment fact, not a sign-up - there is no
# sign-up route on the internal surface at all. Seeded only when no operator
# exists, and flagged so its credential must be changed on first use.
CONTROL_PLANE_BOOTSTRAP_EMAIL=
CONTROL_PLANE_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD=
CONTROL_PLANE_BOOTSTRAP_NAME=Bootstrap operator
